  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41301" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Coastal Community Resilience  to Transnational Organized Crime</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) promoting a whole-of-government dialogue on the human security context in the South coast of the Dominican Republic based on a community-centred and comprehensive analysis of the human security situation in target coastal communities/area with a view to mapping needs, vulnerabilities and capacities to develop strategies aimed at increasing human security levels that be sustainable and that operate in the medium to long-term. 
(2) deliver operational level technical assistance to key partners from within the civilian and law-enforcement communities that can exemplify integrated responses that can prevent Dominican fishermen and coastal communities to spiral down into violence and crime.</narrative>
  </description>
